<title>USA: Bonneville leaves Thursday power offers unchanged.</title>
<headline>Bonneville leaves Thursday power offers unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) left offers for next-day power unchanged, continuing to offer only off-peak supplies, the agency said Wednesday.</p>
<p>For Thursday pre-schedulings, BPA offered non-firm power for hours ending at 0600 and 2300 PDT at $9.50 per megawatt hour (MWh) for both Northwest and COB deliveries, while delivered prices for hours ending 0100-0500 and 2400 were flat at $9.00.</p>
<p>Firm power during off-peak hours on Thursday was also unchanged at $9.00 per MWh for all deliveries.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau +1 212 955 6761))</p>
